<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harpagus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harpagus was a Median noble who, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, saved the infant Cyrus from death ordered by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astyages">Astyages</a> and later helped Cyrus overthrow him around 550 BCE. As Cyrus' general he conquered the Greek cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionia</a>, Caria and Lycia after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a>, around 545–540 BCE. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocaeans">Phocaeans</a> and Teians fled by sea rather than submit, founding new colonies, while the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xanthos">Xanthos</a> fought to the death.</p></div>
